0 1 0 0 0 0 2 1\n0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 2 0\n0 0 0 0 0 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 0 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 2 2 0 0 2 0\n0 0 2 0 2 2 2 0 2 0\n\nYour final answer should just be the python script itself, no other text or markdown.",
  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    # Deep copy to avoid modifying the input\n    g = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    h = len(g)\n    w = len(g[0]) if h else 0\n\n    for col in range(w):\n        # Find the last row of the initial contiguous block of 1's from the top\n        top = -1\n        for row in range(h):\n            if g[row][col] == 1:\n                top = row\n            else:\n                break\n\n        # Count how many 2's are in this column\n        cnt = sum(1 for row in range(h) if g[row][col] == 2)\n        if cnt == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Remove the original 2's\n        for row in range(h):\n            if g[row][col] == 2:\n                g[row][col] = 0\n\n        # Place the 2's right below the block of 1's, preserving order\n        for i in range(cnt):\n            target = top + 1 + i\n            if target < h:\n                g[target][col] = 2\n            # If target is out of bounds, the input is ill\u2011formed; we ignore overflow.\n\n    return g",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    # Deep copy to avoid modifying the input\n    g = [row[:] for row in grid]\n    h = len(g)\n    w = len(g[0]) if h else 0\n\n    for col in range(w):\n        # Find the last row of the initial contiguous block of 1's from the top\n        top = -1\n        for row in range(h):\n            if g[row][col] == 1:\n                top = row\n            else:\n                break\n\n        # Count how many 2's are in this column\n        cnt = sum(1 for row in range(h) if g[row][col] == 2)\n        if cnt == 0:\n            continue\n\n        # Remove the original 2's\n        for row in range(h):\n            if g[row][col] == 2:\n                g[row][col] = 0\n\n        # Place the 2's right below the block of 1's, preserving order\n        for i in range(cnt):\n            target = top + 1 + i\n            if target < h:\n                g[target][col] = 2\n            # If target is out of bounds, the input is ill\u2011formed; we ignore overflow.\n\n    return g",
